.TH DOTFILES-WATCHER 1 "2026-10-29" "1.0.0" "dotfiles-watcher manual"
.SH NAME
dotfiles-watcher \- watch and auto-sync a bare-repo dotfiles setup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dotfiles-watcher
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dotfiles-watcher
monitors all files tracked by the bare git repository at
.I ~/.cfg/
using
.BR entr (1).
When any tracked file changes, it invokes
.B dotfiles-sync
which stages changes, generates an AI commit message via
.BR gemini (1),
and pushes to
.IR origin/main .
.PP
The watcher automatically restarts when the tracked file set changes
(new files added to the repo).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cfg/
Bare git repository tracking dotfiles.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/dotfiles-watcher
Watcher binary.
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/dotfiles-sync
Sync binary (can be run manually).
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/dotfiles-watcher.service
Systemd user service unit.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.BR entr (1),
.BR gemini (1),
.BR git (1)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dotfiles-sync (1),
.BR entr (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
